🚽 Test case: #197 -- chaining `.` through a MULTI-level pointer field
🚽 (`gang Node **next`) is rejected, the field counterpart of #196's
🚽 multi-level pointer VARIABLE rejection. `.` as an implicit `->` only
🚽 makes sense for one level of indirection; `next`'s slot at
🚽 pointer_level 2 holds a `gang Node *`, not a `gang Node` blob, so C
🚽 would require an explicit `(*n.next)->val`.
gang Node {
    rizz val;
    gang Node **next;
};

skibidi main {
    gang Node n;
    n.next.val = 1;
}
